    "text": "# Investigation note: metric M333622, reporting month 2026-10-31\n\n## 1. Executive finding\nM333622 is in the **Amber (watch)** provisional band for 2026-10-31. Its provisional rate is **56.25% (9 of 16)**. That is 18.75 percentage points above the prior month and close to the 60% red boundary. Under the band rule you supplied, where a higher rate is worse, this is a deterioration and the metric is not healthy.\n\n**One thing needs resolving before this finding is used.** The data contradicts the band rule. All 9 numerator rows are Compliant with a passed test. The 7 non-compliant rows are all in the denominator but not the numerator. So the rate tracks the share of compliant rows, which would make a higher rate better. The band's direction should be confirmed before anyone acts on \"Amber\".\n\n## 2. Current status and period (2026-10-31)\n- **Metric rows:** 27, one per application, so 27 applications.\n- **Compliance status:** 9 Compliant, 7 Non_Compliant, 7 Not_Applicable, 4 Pending.\n- **Provisional numerator / denominator:** 9 / 16. The denominator is the 9 Compliant plus the 7 Non_Compliant rows. Pending and Not_Applicable rows are excluded, which matches the inferred EXCLUDES_PENDING scope.\n\n## 3. Movement against 2026-09-30 (provisional)\n- **Rate:** went from 37.5% (6 of 16) to 56.25% (9 of 16). The denominator stayed at 16, so the change comes from the numerator alone (+3).\n- **Non-compliant rows:** fell from 10 to 7. Failed tests fell from 9 to 5.\n- **Application movement (27 applications this month):**\n  - 7 resolved\n  - 3 newly non-compliant\n  - 1 still non-compliant from last month\n  - 6 with no row in the prior month\n  - 10 other\n  - 5 applications reported in September but not October\n- **Who reported changed:** 6 applications joined and 5 left, so part of the rate change may reflect who reported rather than real movement.\n- **12-month range:** the provisional rate moved between 25.0% (2025-11-30) and 66.7% (2026-04-30), so changes from month to month are frequent.\n\n## 4. Main contributors (7 non-compliant rows)\n- **By super division:** Super_Division_04 has 3, Super_Division_05 has 2, and Super_Division_02 and Super_Division_03 have 1 each. Super_Division_01, _06 and _08 have none.\n- **By legal entity:** Legal_Entity_40 is the only one with more than one non-compliant row (2: Application_00381 and Application_01298). Each other legal entity has at most one.\n## 5. Testing and exception observations (2026-10-31)\n- **Completed tests:** 14, of which 9 passed and 5 failed. All 5 failures are non-compliant. The recorded reasons are Test_Failed (3), Open_Findings_Outstanding (1) and Remediation_Overdue (1).\n- **Expired exemptions:** 2 non-compliant rows are marked Exempt with the reason Exemption_Expired. Both are in Super_Division_05 (Application_00689 and Application_00739).\n- **Pending:** 4 rows. 3 are Test_Scheduled and 1 is Awaiting_Test_Assignment. They are outside the denominator.\n- **Not applicable:** 7 rows. 4 are No_Test_Required and 3 are Exemption_Approved.\n\n## 6. Areas for further investigation (hypotheses, not validated)\n- The direction of the band compared with what the numerator actually counts (see section 1).\n- Whether the 3 pending tests, once complete, would change the denominator. Those rows are currently excluded.\n- Whether Super_Division_04 (3 of its 7 rows are non-compliant) has something in common across its applications.\n- Whether the two expired exemptions in Super_Division_05 are being renewed or will be retested. The data shows no remediation status for them.\n- How much of the month's change comes from the 6 applications that joined and the 5 that left.\n\n## 7. Limitations\n- The rate, band, movement and denominator scope are all provisional, and none are confirmed by the client. The meaning of the numerator and denominator has not been supplied.\n- The base is small (16 rows in the denominator), so one application changes the rate by about 6 percentage points.\n- No metric name, metric family, owner or remediation evidence is available. The causes above are not established.\n- All names are synthetic.",
